{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 135, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge into the output adds a new learned path rather than displacing a useful operation."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A residual shortcut from input to output is most valuable when the deep path through node 2 is a stack of 3x3 convolutions."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 1 is absent, removing the input-output shortcut leaves very few paths from the input, starving the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2 absent, deleting edge 0 also disconnects the edge-4 path through node 1, collapsing the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv where there was no edge adds capacity, whereas replacing skip or 1x1 conv on edge 1 discards a useful path."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning an empty node1-to-output edge into a 3x3 conv creates an additional learned path to the output."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the identity link into node 2 with pooling removes clean gradient flow and is more harmful than replacing a conv or empty edge."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is absent, converting the remaining edge-5 conv to identity strips most learned capacity from the output paths."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is empty, edge 4 is a key route to the output, and a parameter-free pooling there regularizes and stabilizes the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the critical input-output residual with a parametric 1x1 conv hurts optimization more than replacing an empty or conv edge."}], "tok": 18165, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"